Task 1: Environment Setup and Tool Installation
Subtask 1.1: Update System and Install Prerequisites
First, update your system and install necessary packages:

sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y
sudo apt install -y curl wget apt-transport-https ca-certificates gnupg lsb-release git
Subtask 1.2: Install Docker
Install Docker Engine on your Linux machine:

# Add Docker's official GPG key
curl -fsSL https://download.docker.com/linux/ubuntu/gpg | sudo gpg --dearmor -o /usr/share/keyrings/docker-archive-keyring.gpg

# Add Docker repository
echo "deb [arch=$(dpkg --print-architecture) signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/docker-archive-keyring.gpg] https://download.docker.com/linux/ubuntu $(lsb_release -cs) stable" | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/docker.list > /dev/null

# Update package index and install Docker
sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y docker-ce docker-ce-cli containerd.io docker-buildx-plugin docker-compose-plugin

# Start and enable Docker service
sudo systemctl start docker
sudo systemctl enable docker

# Add current user to docker group
sudo usermod -aG docker $USER

# Apply group changes
newgrp docker
Verify Docker installation:

docker --version
docker run hello-world
Subtask 1.3: Install Java (Required for Jenkins)
Install OpenJDK 11 which is required for Jenkins:

sudo apt install -y openjdk-11-jdk
java -version
Subtask 1.4: Install Jenkins
Install Jenkins on your system:

# Add Jenkins repository key
curl -fsSL https://pkg.jenkins.io/debian-stable/jenkins.io-2023.key | sudo tee /usr/share/keyrings/jenkins-keyring.asc > /dev/null

# Add Jenkins repository
echo deb [signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/jenkins-keyring.asc] https://pkg.jenkins.io/debian-stable binary/ | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/jenkins.list > /dev/null

# Update package index and install Jenkins
sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y jenkins

# Start and enable Jenkins service
sudo systemctl start jenkins
sudo systemctl enable jenkins
Check Jenkins status:

sudo systemctl status jenkins
Subtask 1.5: Configure Jenkins Initial Setup
Get the initial admin password:

sudo cat /var/lib/jenkins/secrets/initialAdminPassword
Access Jenkins web interface:

# Get your machine's IP address
ip addr show | grep inet
Open a web browser and navigate to http://YOUR_IP_ADDRESS:8080

Complete the Jenkins setup wizard:

Enter the initial admin password
Select Install suggested plugins
Create an admin user account
Configure Jenkins URL (use default)
Click Start using Jenkins
Task 2: Integrate Docker with Jenkins Pipeline
Subtask 2.1: Install Docker Pipeline Plugin
In Jenkins web interface:

Go to Manage Jenkins > Manage Plugins
Click on Available tab
Search for Docker Pipeline
Select the checkbox next to Docker Pipeline
Click Install without restart
Wait for installation to complete
Subtask 2.2: Configure Docker in Jenkins
Add Jenkins user to Docker group:

sudo usermod -aG docker jenkins
sudo systemctl restart jenkins
Verify Docker access for Jenkins:

sudo -u jenkins docker ps
Subtask 2.3: Create Sample Application
Create a directory structure for your sample application:

mkdir -p ~/jenkins-docker-lab
cd ~/jenkins-docker-lab
Create a simple Node.js application:

cat > package.json << 'EOF'
{
  "name": "jenkins-docker-app",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "Sample app for Jenkins Docker integration",
  "main": "app.js",
  "scripts": {
    "start": "node app.js"
  },
  "dependencies": {
    "express": "^4.18.2"
  }
}
EOF
Create the main application file:

cat > app.js << 'EOF'
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
const port = 3000;

app.get('/', (req, res) => {
  res.json({
    message: 'Hello from Jenkins Docker Integration Lab!',
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
    version: '1.0.0'
  });
});

app.get('/health', (req, res) => {
  res.json({ status: 'healthy' });
});

app.listen(port, '0.0.0.0', () => {
  console.log(`App running on port ${port}`);
});
EOF
Create a Dockerfile:

cat > Dockerfile << 'EOF'
FROM node:18-alpine

WORKDIR /app

COPY package*.json ./
RUN npm install --production

COPY . .

EXPOSE 3000

CMD ["npm", "start"]
EOF
Create a .dockerignore file:

cat > .dockerignore << 'EOF'
node_modules
npm-debug.log
.git
.gitignore
README.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
EOF
Subtask 2.4: Initialize Git Repository
Initialize a Git repository for your project:

git init
git config user.name "Jenkins Lab User"
git config user.email "jenkins@lab.local"

cat > .gitignore << 'EOF'
